\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Viability-preserving rollout ADP for orbital inspection. I. International Space Station (ISS) mesh and required targets $\mathcal  K$. II. Camera-valid targets $G_j$ from range, field of view (FOV), incidence $\theta \leq \theta _{\max }$, and line of sight (LOS) checks. III. HCW transfer, motion audits, and directed SOOA construction; C70 and C68 are archived candidate IDs. IV. Depth-$d$ Bellman lookahead with complete greedy base-policy tails. At each leaf, $\DOTSB \sum@ \slimits@ \ell $ denotes the full tail cost; $+\infty $ denotes no certified completion within the remaining budget. V. First-action selection and planning-state updates toward completion of all required targets. The tree is schematic; the 9/9 route is an archived offline plan. ISS geometry: National Aeronautics and Space Administration (NASA), \href  {https://science.nasa.gov/resource/international-space-station-3d-model/}{NASA}.}}{2}{figure.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:sooa-framework}{{1}{2}{Viability-preserving rollout ADP for orbital inspection. I. International Space Station (ISS) mesh and required targets $\mathcal K$. II. Camera-valid targets $G_j$ from range, field of view (FOV), incidence $\theta \leq \theta _{\max }$, and line of sight (LOS) checks. III. HCW transfer, motion audits, and directed SOOA construction; C70 and C68 are archived candidate IDs. IV. Depth-$d$ Bellman lookahead with complete greedy base-policy tails. At each leaf, $\sum \ell $ denotes the full tail cost; $+\infty $ denotes no certified completion within the remaining budget. V. First-action selection and planning-state updates toward completion of all required targets. The tree is schematic; the 9/9 route is an archived offline plan. ISS geometry: National Aeronautics and Space Administration (NASA), \href {https://science.nasa.gov/resource/international-space-station-3d-model/}{NASA}}{figure.3}{}}
